---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { GOSPEL_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE, STUDIO_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`The Gospel | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description={GOSPEL_DESCRIPTION}
		/>
	</head>
	<body class="gospel-page">
		<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
		<SiteHeader />
		<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
			<header class="gospel-intro" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">The Gospel</p>
				<h1>Good news of Jesus Christ.</h1>
				<p class="gospel-intro__lead">
					The gospel is God's good news: sinners can be reconciled to their holy Creator through
					the life, death, and bodily resurrection of Jesus Christ.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section class="gospel-section" aria-labelledby="gospel-creation-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">God and creation</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-creation-title">We belong to our holy Creator.</h2>
					<p>
						God is holy and righteous, the Creator of everything. He made human beings in His
						image, with dignity, and for relationship with Him (Genesis 1:1, 1:26-27). All creation
						belongs to Him, and our lives are accountable to our Maker.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-section gospel-section--light" aria-labelledby="gospel-sin-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Humanity and sin</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-sin-title">Sin separates us from God.</h2>
					<p>
						All people have sinned and fall short of God's righteousness (Romans 3:23). Sin is
						more than individual mistakes: it is our rebellion against God, expressed in the
						choices and desires that turn us from Him. We cannot reconcile ourselves to God by
						good intentions or moral effort; sin brings real guilt and separation (Romans 6:23;
						Isaiah 59:2).
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-section" aria-labelledby="gospel-christ-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Jesus Christ</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-christ-title">Jesus died and rose to save sinners.</h2>
					<p>
						Jesus Christ is the Son of God. He lived without sin, died on the cross for our sins,
						was buried, and bodily rose from the dead on the third day (1 Corinthians 15:3-4;
						Hebrews 4:15). In His death He bore sin's judgment; in His resurrection He conquered
						sin and death. God showed His love for us in that Christ died for us while we were
						still sinners (Romans 5:8).
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-section gospel-section--light" aria-labelledby="gospel-grace-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Grace and salvation</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-grace-title">Salvation is God's gift, not our achievement.</h2>
					<p>
						We are saved by God's grace through faith in Jesus Christ, not by works, moral
						improvement, or religious activity (Ephesians 2:8-9). God calls us to repent—to turn
						from sin—and to trust Christ as Lord and Savior (Mark 1:15; Romans 10:9-10). We receive
						forgiveness because of what Jesus has done, not because we have earned it.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-section gospel-section--invitation" aria-labelledby="gospel-response-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Respond to Christ</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-response-title">Repent and believe in Jesus.</h2>
					<p>
						Turn from sin and put your trust in Jesus Christ as Lord and Savior. Call on Him for
						mercy, trusting His death and resurrection rather than your own effort. Scripture
						promises that everyone who calls on the name of the Lord will be saved (Romans 10:13).
						This is an invitation to come to Christ, not a formula or a promise that following
						Him will remove every hardship.
					</p>
					<div class="gospel-next-steps">
						<h3>Begin following Jesus.</h3>
						<p>
							Read the Bible, beginning with one of the Gospels; pray honestly to God; speak
							with a faithful local church about baptism; join a community of believers; and
							grow in obedience to Christ with the help of His people (Matthew 28:19-20;
							2 Timothy 3:16-17; Hebrews 10:24-25).
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="gospel-callout" aria-labelledby="gospel-questions-title" data-reveal>
				<p class="eyebrow">Questions and conversation</p>
				<div>
					<h2 id="gospel-questions-title">We would be glad to hear from you.</h2>
					<p>
						If you have questions about Christianity or following Jesus, contact us at
						<a href={`mailto:${STUDIO_EMAIL}`}>{STUDIO_EMAIL}</a> or use the contact page.
						We encourage you to speak with a local church as you explore the Christian faith.
					</p>
					<div class="gospel-callout__actions">
						<a class="button button--primary" href="/contact/">Ask a question</a>
						<a class="button button--quiet" href={`mailto:${STUDIO_EMAIL}?subject=Question%20about%20the%20gospel`}>
							Email Petalwake <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</body>
</html>
